# shell: both
# FS-060/FS-055: the clipboard entry follows the file it names, so a second
# paste copies what the first one moved.  Nothing followed a move before:
# the entry still named the old path, the file was no longer there, and the
# second paste pruned the entry instead of pasting it.
wait 6
note a.txt is cut and pasted into sub, which MOVES it
click-row 1
wait 2
key x ctrl
wait 3
click-row 0
click-row 0
wait 10
expect-title sub
key v ctrl
wait 40
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/sub/a.txt
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_script/a.txt
note the entry went with it.  Back in the folder it came from, a second
note paste copies the file from where it is NOW -- an entry left naming the
note old path would be pruned here and nothing would arrive
key Up ctrl alt
wait 10
expect-title trk_script
key v ctrl
wait 40
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/a.txt
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/sub/a.txt
note and a RENAME is the same event: the entry still names the file in sub,
note so renaming that file has to take the entry with it
click-row 0
click-row 0
wait 10
expect-title sub
click-row 0
wait 45
click-row 0
wait 120
expect-renaming 1
key k
key e
key p
key t
key Return
wait 40
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/sub/kept
key Up ctrl alt
wait 10
expect-title trk_script
key v ctrl
wait 40
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/kept
quit
